1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,560
Legend says this con man sold the Eiffel Tower for scrap.

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:07,440
His name? Victor Lustig, and he called himself a count.

3
00:00:07,980 --> 00:00:10,600
That's a noble title, but his was made up.

4
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:13,420
Here's the story. Paris, nineteen twenty-five.

5
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:16,000
He pretends to be a government official.

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,280
Then he invites five scrap-metal dealers to a hotel.

7
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:22,580
Scrap is old metal they melt down, then sell again.

8
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:26,780
Now he tells them, quietly, the tower's being sold for scrap.

9
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:28,920
Hit like if you'd have walked right out.

10
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:33,220
One dealer, Poisson, reportedly paid, and Lustig left with the cash.

11
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,360
And Poisson? He was too embarrassed to call the police.

12
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:39,960
So then, legend says, he came back and tried again.

13
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:43,140
But no court ever proved any of that. It's a legend.

14
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,720
Send this to the friend who'd buy the Eiffel Tower.

15
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:48,940
So what's actually on the record? Fake money.

16
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:52,840
In America, he got into counterfeiting, which means making fake cash.

17
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:56,100
In May nineteen thirty-five, he was arrested in New York.

18
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:59,680
Here's who caught him: the Secret Service, who chase fake money.

19
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:03,460
Then he escaped from a federal jail, and was caught weeks later.

20
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:06,360
Follow if you love a legend meeting the real record.

21
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:10,460
He pleaded guilty: fifteen years for that, plus five for the escape.

22
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:15,040
That's twenty years, at Alcatraz, the famous island prison.

23
00:01:15,060 --> 00:01:17,080
Twenty years is longer than a whole childhood.

24
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:20,600
And the twist? He was never even charged for the Eiffel Tower.

25
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,480
The legend made him famous. But the fake money locked him up.

26
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:27,160
Real con or tall tale? One word.

